Kairyu vendors and adapts the 25 instruction checkers under the Apache License,
Version 2.0. Adaptations include package-relative imports, standard-library
logging, deterministic langdetect seeding, and a pure-function evaluation facade.
The official strict/loose response transformations are retained.

Dataset-consistency amendment: pinned IFEval keys 1122 and 1129 require the
characters `#` and `!`. Upstream LetterFrequencyChecker silently replaces both
with a random ASCII letter, independently for strict and loose evaluation.
Kairyu preserves any non-whitespace single character and rejects invalid letter
arguments, so both arms score the constraint encoded by the pinned dataset.
